#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Break src/simsui/ on purpose and check simsuidiff reports each break.

    python3 -B tools/simsui_breaks.py [scenarios] [name...]

Only a reported DIFFER counts as caught: a build failure, a fault or a timeout does not.
Run from a frozen copy of the tree if the sources may change meanwhile (copy first, then
run there), as tools/flights_breaks.py says for Flights.

Left out as proven equivalent:
- CDIBSection's operator HBITMAP testing its CBitmap's address for null (this + 0x5c is null
  only for an object at 0xffffffa4).
- load-flip (LoadDib negating a bottom-up height): CreateDib, which it calls next with the same
  header, negates any positive height before anything reads it, and the header is LoadDib's own.
- clip-negative, clip-dest-y (the order of two writes in ClipRects): they differ only when the
  two pointers alias; for source_x == width the negative value makes the sum negative and the
  routine returns first; for dest_y == source_y both writes store 0.
- clip-height (>= against >): at equality the height written is the height already there.
- tile-left-width (the middle rows' left count read again from the section): it is the width
  read at entry; Tile writes only the destination's bits, never a section's header.
- blit-attrib (GetDeviceCaps on m_hAttribDC against m_hDC): CDC::Attach sets both to the one
  handle, and Blt's DC is attached just before.
- 3piece-init-two-top (/ 2 against >> 1 for a two-line text's top): they differ only for a
  negative odd value, and every negative top is clamped to 0.
- check-init-height, tab-height, init-tile-height (a BITMAPINFO's height negated): CreateDib,
  which every one of these headers goes to, negates any positive height, so h and -h both
  reach CreateDIBSection as -|h|.
- paint-attrib (the group box's text measured on m_hDC against m_hAttribDC): CPaintDC
  attaches the one handle as both.
- shadow-hard (flags & 0x30 against & 0x20): it is the else of flags & 0x10, so bit 0x10 is clear
  and the two tests agree.
Caught only at more scenarios: 3piece-init-rest (scenario 1016 of 3piece_init alone),
command-seven-same (N=2000: OnCommand's EN_KILLFOCUS-like case 7 with the focus on the edit
being validated).
"""
from pathlib import Path
import re
import subprocess
